        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(sakana): surface pay-as-you-go credit balance",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Fetch Sakana subscription quota and the optional pay-as-you-go tab concurrently with the same normalized cookie header.\n- Keep subscription quota authoritative: PAYG network, status, redirect, and parse failures only omit the optional enrichment.\n- Bound enrichment with a shared 200 ms merge budget, a finite operation lifetime, and explicit cancellation when the required fetch fails.\n- Parse the real server-rendered balance, usage total, and date range, including React hydration comments.\n- Show Balance and Recent usage only when optional usage is enabled; toggling it off also hides already-cached PAYG rows immediately.\n- Document the two-request behavior and add the 0.38.1 changelog entry with contributor credit.\n\nDepends on #1873 for reliable bounded Gemini package-discovery subprocesses already present in this branch ancestry.\n\n## Proof\n\n- `swift test --filter SakanaUsageFetcherTests` — 23/23 passed.\n- `swift test --filter MenuDescriptorSakanaTests` — 2/2 passed.\n- `make check` — repository guards, links, locale parity, SwiftFormat, and SwiftLint passed.\n- Live authenticated Sakana billing markup verified by the contributor: the PAYG cards are server-rendered only for `?tab=payAsYouGo`; no guessed response shape.\n- Structured autoreview — clean on the parser/concurrency implementation; latest render-gating follow-up reviewed manually and covered by focused tests.\n\n## Risk\n\nLow to medium and provider-scoped. The required subscription result never waits more than the bounded enrichment budget, optional failures remain contained, and cached optional rows obey the current setting at render time.\n",
